# Trust anchors for www.puc.texas.gov (PUCT calendar source).
#
# ROOT CAUSE (corrected 2026-08-18 after adversarial review): PUC's chain
# terminates at the "AAA Certificate Services" root (Comodo, 2004), which
# Mozilla retired and certifi REMOVED in its 2025.6.15 release — so a
# fresh `pip install` on the GitHub runner has no trust anchor for this
# site at all ("unable to get local issuer certificate", build #99).
# The server serves its chain correctly; local openssl checks passed only
# because `openssl verify` also consults the system store, which (like
# Apple's and Microsoft's) still ships this root.
#
# sources/puct.py appends this file to certifi for ITS requests only:
# the retired root below is the required anchor, and the four
# intermediates ride along so verification succeeds even if the server
# omits its chain. Deliberate, contained re-trust of a root retired for
# age/policy (not compromise).
#
# HARD DEADLINE: the root and both SSL.com transit CAs expire
# 2028-12-31; PUC/Cloudflare must re-chain before then. puct.py starts
# flagging a health problem in late 2028 as the tripwire, and this file
# should be deleted once PUC's chain reaches a root certifi still ships.

